{"source_key":"sha256-1b040a14b56f8e8c10dd28d48155f19f","record_index":217,"record_hash":"sha256:11f3fb862022e939bf17c49d739a41c7fad922d98ef4c7a140d3a51966e45516","timestamp":"2026-07-09T12:09:57.255Z","kind":"message","source_event_kind":"codex:response_item:message","role":"user","text":"<subagent_notification>\n{\"agent_path\":\"[REDACTED:entropy]\",\"status\":{\"completed\":\"Read the required docs first and inspected `caleb/single-branch-project-starting` read-only. No files edited; I did not run tests.\\n\\n**1. CLI Call**\\nThe reusable plumbing is `but_workspace::init::set_target_ref_and_init_project()` in [init.rs]([REDACTED:path]), but CLI should go through `but-api`, not call workspace plumbing directly.\\n\\nFor CLI paths that already hold `RepoExclusive`, the branch is missing the ideal reusable API: `but_api::workspace::set_target_ref_and_init_project_with_perm(...)`. The existing API wrapper self-locks at [workspace.rs]([REDACTED:path]), so it is fine for Tauri/NAPI/server calls, but not for CLI code already holding a permission token.\\n\\nCurrent CLI gaps:\\n- `but setup` still calls legacy `set_base_branch_with_perm()` at [setup.rs]([REDACTED:path]).\\n- `but config target` still calls legacy `set_base_branch()` at [config.rs]([REDACTED:path]).\\n\\nCLI should pass a full ref like `refs/remotes/origin/main`, plus optional push remote.\\n\\n**2. Data And Permissions**\\nNeeds:\\n- `&mut Context` at the API boundary.\\n- `RepoExclusive` because it writes repo-local config and legacy metadata.\\n- `target_ref: &gix::refs::FullNameRef`, required to be an existing remote-tracking ref.\\n- optional `push_remote`, validated if present.\\n- repo-local Git config write access for `gitbutler.project.*` and `log.excludeDecoration`.\\n- writable `RefMetadata` so `ProjectMeta::persist()` can backfill legacy workspace metadata at [ref_metadata.rs]([REDACTED:path]).\\n- workspace cache invalidation after write, as the API does at [workspace.rs]([REDACTED:path]).\\n\\nIt deliberately does not create stacks, checkout `gitbutler/workspace`, create a workspace ref, or write an oplog snapshot.\\n\\n**3. Coverage**\\nGood coverage:\\n- workspace init tests cover fresh init preserving current branch, no workspace ref, target metadata, `log.excludeDecoration`, push remote preservation, and validation failures in [init.rs]([REDACTED:path]).\\n- API tests cover remote ref acceptance, local branch rejection, and merge-base behavior in [workspace.rs]([REDACTED:path]).\\n- e2e covers single-branch onboarding keeping `master`, preserving dirty worktree, avoiding workspace ref creation, and writing `targetRef` in [addingAProject.spec.ts]([REDACTED:path]).\\n- server/SDK exposure exists at [but-server/src/lib.rs]([REDACTED:path]) and [index.d.ts]([REDACTED:path]).\\n\\nGaps:\\n- no CLI coverage for the new path.\\n- no direct test for the operating-mode fallback that keeps `branch_name` when conflict computation fails.\\n- no downstream projection test for changing target ref after a target commit id already exists.\\n\\n**4. Correctness Risks**\\nMain risk: changing target ref preserves the old `target_commit_id` by design at [init.rs]([REDACTED:path]), and the test locks that in at [init.rs]([REDACTED:path]). That is good for idempotent init/migration, but risky for real target switching in single-branch mode, because `targetRef = origin/release` with an old `origin/main` commit id can skew graph/base calculations.\\n\\nSmallest fix: preserve the commit id only when the existing target ref equals the requested target ref; recompute merge-base when the target ref actually changes.\\n\\nSecondary risk: `ProjectMeta::resolve()` errors are swallowed at [init.rs]([REDACTED:path]), which can silently drop existing push remote/target state on metadata read failures. Fine for “no metadata yet,” too broad for corrupted or inaccessible metadata.\\n\\nSkipped: no edits, no validation run; this was inspection only.\\n\\n\"}}\n<[REDACTED:path]>","prompt_source":"system_injected","tool_name":null,"tool_input":null,"source_record":{"timestamp":"2026-07-09T12:09:57.255Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"user","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"[REDACTED:entropy]"}}}}